// Minimal file carrying a preprocessor directive, for test_fmt_directive_stdout.
//
// `lls fmt` refuses files like this: it cannot see the tokens inside inactive
// #if branches, so reformatting them is unsafe. The point of the test is that
// refusing must still pass the source through verbatim in --stdout mode --
// writing nothing there destroys the file in any pipeline use.
//
// Keep this file ASCII-only. The driver compares the source against the tool's
// stdout through CMake execute_process, which re-encodes non-ASCII bytes; an em
// dash in a comment shows up as a false mismatch even when the pass-through is
// byte-correct. (That is exactly why this sample exists instead of reusing
// condcomp_test.lls, which has one.)

#if WINDOWS
def platform_tag() -> int { return 1 }
#else
def platform_tag() -> int { return 2 }
#endif

def main() {
    @print(platform_tag())
}
